  "question": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math> upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>78</mn></math> terms and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8230;</mo></math> upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>59</mn></math> terms be two series. Then, the sum of the terms common to both the series is equal to ______.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "2223",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></math> upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>78</mn></math> terms</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>78</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>77</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>234</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo></math> upto <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>59</mn></math> terms</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>59</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>58</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>237</mn></math></p><p>Common difference of common terms&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>LCM</mi><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>12</mn></math></p><p>First common term is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and last common term is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>225</mn></math></p><p>So series will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>21</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>33</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#8943;</mo><mo>,</mo><mn>225</mn></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>19</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>S</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>19</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>225</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2223</mn></math></p>",
